<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sukkur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sukkur is a city on the right bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, opposite Rohri. Nearby lay <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aror">Aror</a>, capital of medieval Sindh. The Sukkur Barrage, completed in 1932 under British rule, feeds one of the largest irrigation systems in the world, and the city is an important river crossing and market.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sukkur.jpg" alt="Sukkur" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ibaadnaqvi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rohri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
